    <p class="muted small" style="margin:10px 0 0">When this version was built (19 November 2026), the calculation behind this page was also re-solved independently with NumPy and SciPy. For 16 loads the line load was written as a function along the beam and integrated numerically, which gives the size and the place of the resultant without the formulas of this page. The reactions were then found from the load itself, sampled at eight points along its length, with the balance of forces and the balance of moments about a point that is on neither support solved as one set of equations. All 80 comparisons agreed to better than one part in a billion. What was not done is a comparison with a measurement on a beam.</p>
